course: dictionary
lesson: 11580
title: Anonymously: giving without a name
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Anonymously is an adverb. It tells us how something is done: without a name, so nobody knows who did it. «She donated money to the hospital anonymously.» The word anonymously tells you she gave the money, but her name was kept secret.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «The note was signed anonymously, so nobody knew who had written it.» If the writer's name is missing or hidden, the word anonymously is probably the answer. Ask yourself: is the person's name a secret here?
explain: You can also use the word about safety. «You can report bullying anonymously, so your name stays secret.» This means you can tell an adult about a problem without anyone knowing it was you. Words like anonymous, anonymity and anonymously all come from the same idea: no name.
fact: Anonymously means without giving your name, so nobody knows who you are.
fact: The adjective is anonymous, as in «an anonymous gift», meaning a gift with no name on it.
fact: Useful phrases: give anonymously, donate anonymously, report anonymously, remain anonymous.
fact: «Anonymously» can also mean in a way that hides who someone is, even if the name is partly known.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «without giving my name» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «He gave the money to the school anonymously.» What does anonymously mean here? | *Without giving his name | With a big smile and a loud speech | In a paper bag | Very quickly
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that tells us the name was kept secret: «The letter was signed anonymously, so nobody knew who wrote it.» | wrote | knew | *anonymously | letter
exercise: Lily wants to tell her teacher about a problem, but she does not want anyone to know it was her. Lily reported the problem ___. Which word fits best? | happily | loudly | slowly | *anonymously
test: «Ben gave a book to the library anonymously.» What does this tell us? | The book was very old | *The gift came with no name | Ben read the book quickly | Ben was very tall
test: Which phrase means the same as anonymously? | *Without giving your name | Very loudly | At the front of the line | In a hurry
exam: Mia donated money to the animal shelter ___, so no one knows it was her. Which word fits best? | *anonymously | proudly | nervously | angrily
